# YouTube Downloader — First-Time Setup

## 1. Download

Grab the latest release from GitHub. You need these files together in the **same folder**:

- `YouTubeDownloader.exe`
- `ffmpeg` folder
- `YouTubeDownloaderUpdater` folder

## 2. Folder layout

When you're done, the folder should look like this:

```
YouTubeDownloader\
├── YouTubeDownloader.exe
├── ffmpeg\
│   └── (ffmpeg.exe, ffprobe.exe, etc.)
└── YouTubeDownloaderUpdater\
    └── (YouTubeDownloaderUpdater.exe, etc.)
```

Don't rename or move any of these — the app looks for them right next to itself.

## 3. Run it

Double-click `YouTubeDownloader.exe`. Paste in a YouTube URL, pick your settings, and hit Download.

## 4. Updates

Click **Check for Updates** any time to get the latest version. Updates install automatically — the app will close briefly and reopen on its own.

---

**Note:** If the `YouTubeDownloaderUpdater` folder is missing when you try to update, the app will automatically download and set it up for you — no manual steps needed.
